        <!--
          THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH, BUT NOT THE FILE SPARKLE READS. The monorepo is
          private, so its raw.githubusercontent URLs 404 for an installed app. release.sh
          mirrors this file into the PUBLIC bronty13/phantomlives-releases repo, and the
          app's SUFeedURL points THERE. Never repoint a feed at this repo — that is the
          stranding failure documented in docs/update-stranding.md.

          Publish a release with ./Scripts/release.sh (see RELEASING.md) — in practice via
          `./release-on-airy.sh PurplePeek` from the repo root, since releases are cut on
          the runner. It builds + notarizes + zips the app, EdDSA-signs the zip, creates a
          tagged GitHub release on the public repo, prepends an <item> here, commits it, and
          mirrors it. Do not hand-edit the items below.

          No <item> yet: PurplePeek has never been released. Sparkle treats an item-less
          feed as "no update available", which is the correct answer until the first
          release lands.
        -->
